{
  "fixtureVersion": 1,
  "id": "read-update-aliases",
  "description": "The two alias targets: a put that creates an alias to a canonical Bead, a put that repoints it, a retry that returns the retained disposition, a put to the target the alias already has, a Bead creation refused on the live alias path with alias-path-taken, a delete that releases the path, a put that reuses it, the same key presented with a different target (an idempotency conflict), a Link created at the path beside the live alias (Link segments and alias paths coexist), one sequence that creates a Bead and then binds its alias through @name, and the refusals — an alias, a Link, and an external URI as a put's target, a committed Bead's path, an unknown target, an unknown alias on delete, an alias member beneath the wrong root, and a delete whose current target the principal cannot see. No target Bead changes revision anywhere here: alias mutation mints no version. Conditions are narrated, not observed. Illustrative wire example; not evidence.",
  "scope": "https://beads.example/acme/",
  "exchanges": [
    {
      "id": "put-alias-creates",
      "condition": "No alias is at alias/adr/sequence-envelopes and no canonical Bead segment has the path adr/sequence-envelopes. decision-7 is at decision-7-r7 before the put and after it.",
